# Force LF line endings for everything git treats as text, regardless
# of core.autocrlf on any given machine. Without this, a Windows
# checkout (core.autocrlf=true, common default on Git for Windows)
# gets CRLF on disk while the repo stores LF — harmless for most tools,
# but prettier's --check (services/web) correctly flags that mismatch
# as "unformatted" even though nothing is actually wrong, which made
# `npm run format:check` fail on every file on a fresh Windows clone.
* text=auto eol=lf
